  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Employers&#x2019; organisations are central to mobilizing the voice of private sector enterprises as the principal source of economic growth, job creation and decent work, and are an indispensable component of democratic and inclusive governance. Employers&#x2019; organisations have an essential role in leading economic and social change and advocating for policies to promote an enabling environment for sustainable enterprises and shared prosperity. Effective exercise of this role involves strengthening the independence and good governance of Employers&#x2019; organisations; increasing alliances with like-minded partners, such as other representative business organizations; and expanding their membership to enhance their representativity. Employers&#x2019; organisations require enhanced capabilities to respond to membership needs through inclusive and transparent organizational governance and functional performance, and the provision of relevant services. 

The interventions is focusing on providing entry points for ILO engagement with the private sector, including through initiatives such as the ILO Global Business Network on Forced Labour and increasing their representativeness and their ability to speak on behalf of the private sector as a whole, advocating for evidence-based, data-driven policy reforms and leading improvements in the business climate and productivity growth. The governance challenges, becoming data-driven organizations by promoting a culture of innovation that positions data at the centre of the employers&#x2019; organization strategy and decision-making and participating and influencing United Nations development processes, including United Nations Cooperation Framework and annual updates of the Common Country Analysis.  

Beneficiaries of this intervention include employers of Mozambique especially those in the private sector. The intervention is being implemented in collaboration with Employers&#x2019; and Workers&#x2019; Organisations, sector Associations, and private sector.</narrative>
  </description>
